cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GLIDER: General Laboratory Interface for Design, Experimentation,
  and Recording
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and
  the accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bradham
    given-names: Garrett
    email: gbradham@go.olemiss.edu
    affiliation: University of Mississippi
  - name: Laing Lab
    address: University of Mississippi
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-07'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/LaingLab/glider'
url: 'https://github.com/LaingLab/glider'
abstract: >-
  GLIDER is a cross-platform desktop application for laboratory
  automation. It combines visual flow programming for experimental
  protocols, direct hardware control over Arduino, Raspberry Pi and PC
  interfaces, multi-camera capture with pose tracking, frame-wise
  behavior classification, and timestamped synchronization with
  external acquisition systems such as fiber photometry.
keywords:
  - laboratory automation
  - behavioral neuroscience
  - pose estimation
  - behavior classification
  - fiber photometry
  - open-source scientific software
